@anon.e792752b4454889dead1a66caae2c60f.1112 = private unnamed_addr constant [862 x i8] c"Force `import from` statements with multiple members and at least one\0Aalias (e.g., `import A as B`) to wrap such that every line contains\0Aexactly one member. For example, this formatting would be retained,\0Arather than condensing to a single line:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom .utils import (\0A    test_directory as test_directory,\0A    test_id as test_id\0A)\0A```\0A\0ANote that this setting is only effective when combined with\0A`combine-as-imports = true`. When [`combine-as-imports`](#lint_isort_combine-as-imports) isn't\0Aenabled, every aliased `import from` will be given its own line, in\0Awhich case, wrapping is not necessary.\0A\0AWhen using the formatter, ensure that [`format.skip-magic-trailing-comma`](#format_skip-magic-trailing-comma) is set to `false` (default)\0Awhen enabling `force-wrap-aliases` to avoid that the formatter collapses members if they all fit on a single line.", align 1
